 {
  "question": "Why do subscribers cancel, and what could keep them?",
  "text": "Based on Q2 2026 cancellation data, subscribers cancel for the following reasons [customers/subscription-churn-q2-2026.md]:\n\n* **Too much coffee at home**: 41%\n* **Price**: 23%\n* **Moving or travelling**: 14%\n* **Taste**: 9%\n* **Other**: 13%\n\n### What could keep them:\n* **A pause option**: Most subscribers leaving due to volume would have stayed if offered a pause option [customers/subscription-churn-q2-2026.md]. Specifically, offering a one- or two-month pause on the cancellation page, or switching to delivery every two weeks, could keep subscribers who have excess coffee [ideas/pause-instead-of-cancel.md]. Similar shops report retaining a third of people who intended to cancel using this method [ideas/pause-instead-of-cancel.md].\n\n*(Note: The notes do not provide solutions or retention ideas for the other cancellation reasons, such as price, moving/travelling, or taste.)*",
