 {
  "question": "How is a subscription order roasted and shipped?",
  "text": "Subscription orders follow a weekly schedule [operations/shipping/subscription-packing-day.md]:\n\n1. **Roasting (Monday)**: Every coffee needed for the week's subscriptions is roasted [operations/shipping/subscription-packing-day.md]. Quality checks include cupping each batch the next morning against a reference sample and measuring ground coffee colour with Agtron [operations/roasting/quality-control-and-cupping.md].\n2. **Packing (Tuesday morning)**: Bags are packed and labeled (around 420 bags per week) [operations/shipping/subscription-packing-day.md].\n3. **Shipping (Tuesday at 15:00)**: The carrier collects the parcels [operations/shipping/subscription-packing-day.md, operations/shipping/carriers-and-delivery-times.md]. \n\nDelivery takes 1–2 working days for Italy and 3–5 working days for the European Union [operations/shipping/carriers-and-delivery-times.md]. Specific roast profiles depend on the bean (for example, the reference profile for Aurora uses a 12 kg batch on the 15 kg roaster with a 205 °C charge and a drop at 11:30) [operations/roasting/aurora-roast-profile.md].",
